cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Reflex-1, please cite it as below."
title: "Reflex-1: frontier-LLM accuracy at Jev speed with a 4B open model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Suzuki
    given-names: Gosuke
    affiliation: Suzuki Shoten
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/matu79go/reflex-1"
url: "https://huggingface.co/matu79go/Reflex-1-4B"
abstract: >-
  Reflex-1 is a 4B open decision model built on Google Gemma 4 E4B for routing,
  guardrails and classification. It returns a choice with probabilities instead of
  generated text. In instant mode it reads option probabilities in a single forward
  pass and matches the accuracy band of frontier LLMs (GPT-5.6, Gemini 3.8) and the
  dedicated judgment API Jev on five public classification benchmarks, at 0.10 s
  median latency on one GPU; it also classifies images. In deep mode, trained per
  judgment, it solves decisions that require reasoning through latent reasoning,
  with each latent step supervised through the model's shared LM head so that it
  can be decoded back into words, reaching frontier-level accuracy at about one
  second per question on trained tasks.
keywords:
  - decision model
  - latent reasoning
  - small language model
  - classification
  - Gemma
